''This article is about the enemy. For the cat unit, see [[Killer Cowbird Cat (Rare Cat)]].''

'''Killer Cowbird Cat''' (殺意のウシネコノトリ, ''Satsui no Ushinekonotori'', '''Killer Cow Cat Bird''') is a [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy. It was added in [[Version 15.2 Update|Version 15.2]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Killer Cowbird Cat
|image = E 770.png
|first appearance = [[Horde of Cats]]
|money drop = 250¢ - 987¢
}}

==Enemy==
This Dark/Floating menace strikes from afar with somewhat frequent [[Long Distance]] attacks reaching all the way to 470 range, while having a small blindspot that even melee attackers struggle to infiltrate, which can easily compound in many of its appearances where it is buffed beyond belief, hiding behind massive swarms of durable threats as it whittles away at the frontline with impunity. Its only notable weaknesses are its relatively long attack cycle, Single Attack and two easily exploitable traits, allowing for a wide variety of accessible counters.

==Strategy==
While their stats seem unimpressive, they are always seen at extremely high magnifications, making them a threatening nuisance. They also appear alongside the rest of the Killer Cats, creating a self-defending wall of enemies. However, their shared [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] trait makes them vulnerable to units such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] if you have them. While they do possess a blind spot, it is small and protected by the other enemies present such as [[Killer Tank Cat (Enemy)|Killer Tank Cat]], and thus it is often best to ignore this weakness and focus on their other big weakness: Single Attack. As they can only hit one cat at a time, heavy use of meatshields such as [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] and [[Kabuto Cat (Special Cat)|Kabuto Cat]] can be a lifesaver.

